 "description": "Find out whether an agent can actually choose correctly within a toolset. Reports pairs of tools whose words overlap enough to be confusable, descriptions too short or too empty to distinguish, undescribed arguments an agent must guess at, tools with so many arguments they are filled wrong, state-changing tools with no annotation hints, and the total size of the manifest, which occupies the model context on every turn. Pay 180000 atomic USDC on Base via exact x402. MCP does not pay; it provides a challenge handoff.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "max_manifest_characters": {
    "description": "Budget for the total size of all tool definitions. Defaults to 20000. Every character sits in the model context on every turn.",
    "example": 2000,
    "minimum": 500,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "min_description_characters": {
    "description": "Shortest description that can distinguish a tool. Defaults to 20.",
    "minimum": 0,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "toolset": {
    "description": "An MCP toolset: either the tools/list result object, or the bare array of tool definitions. At most 400 tools are read and the rest are reported. A capabilities or serverInfo object is used when present. Nothing is fetched and no tool is ever called.",
    "example": {
     "tools": [
      {
       "description": "Fetch a user record by id.",
